In article <1992Feb10.203615.24735@ux1.cso.uiuc.edu> act31797@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu (The Procrastinator) writes:
>>BTW, how do you know when you're invisible when you have the intrinsic
>>see invisible?  Or can you know (short of getting an intrinsics list)?
>
>	When you're invisible, your character symbol "@" will disappear,
>leaving just a cursor.  When you gain the intrinsic see invisible, your char-
>acter symbol will reappear.  (I.e. you will be able to see yourself again.)

It is possible to have the "see invisible" intrinsic at the time of obtaining
the "invisibility" intrinsic.  In this case, the above doesn't work.  You can
always see yourself.  A good indicator of invisiblity is how the monsters
react to you.  If they behave like they can't see you, they probably can't.
If you can see yourself when it appears that they can't see you, you are
invisible and can see invisible.

